Thinking: ADR-014 promises that qualitative evidence describes one exact GGUF, so checking its bytes only before a long run leaves a time-of-check/time-of-use gap. Rehashing after the server exits and requiring equality catches ordinary cache replacement or symlink retargeting during the run. The role-play rule now also requires both a modern-device reference and an explicit unavailability phrase, avoiding a bare 'have no' false positive while retaining common period-appropriate refusals.
